      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": "66399f6107e47e87a33acfbe",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Show the Group owner on its Group detail page if the group is public.\n\nWhen you find an interesting group but are unsure it is \"reliable\", the owner's information could be an excellent source to determine.\n\nOf course, owners can describe the group well on their \"About This Group\". If the system shows the owner's information, it is more dependable because it is not imitable.\n\nCurrently, you can only see who the owner is after joining. And the group might refuse your join request. You can't know (or investigate) in that case.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Show the Group owner on the Group detail page",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "63881d8d39bd597fed3c42a7",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In the Japanese community on VRChat, there is an ongoing discussion about GroupPublic's autonomy. From this point of view, Group owner information is very important. Currently, when joining a GroupPublic, it is not possible to check the owner's information, which is a growing problem.\n\nIt is very important to be able to see the owner information of open Groups that you are not a member of on the VRChat in-game screen.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
